==English==

===Proverb===
{{infl|en|proverb|head=[[to]] [[thine]] [[own]] [[self]] [[be]] [[true]]}}

# A [[cliché]] used to remind people that the easiest person to deceive is oneself.
#: ''"This above all:
#: '''to thine own self be true''',
#: and it must follow, as the night the day,
#: Thou canst not then be false to any man."''  -William Shakespeare

